.TH "mbedded\-cbor\-schema" "7" "2026-11-08" "mbedded\-cbor 0.9.0" "mbedded\-cbor"
.SH Schema
A plain CBOR message carries its keys and its structure in every
message.
To read one field, a reader walks over the items before it.
\f[CR]cbor::schema<T>\f[R] removes that walk.
It writes a struct as Packed CBOR (draft\-ietf\-cbor\-packed\-19): the
struct is the layout, a field of fixed size sits at an offset that the
compiler computes, and a read goes to that offset directly.
FlatBuffers and Cap\(aqn Proto work the same way, but the message stays
CBOR: a decoder of Packed CBOR reads it as a map with the names of the
members as keys.
.PP
