.PP
Every read checks the bytes that it reads.
A read never goes outside the message, and a field with a wrong head
gives an error.
.SS 8. Read from a peer that you trust
\f[CR]unverified_path\f[R], \f[CR]unverified_at_path\f[R] and
\f[CR]unverified_decode\f[R] take the same arguments as \f[CR]path\f[R],
\f[CR]at_path\f[R] and \f[CR]decode\f[R].
They do not check the tags and the heads in the message.
They check every bound, so a read never goes outside the message.
A wrong byte gives a wrong value, not an error.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]auto\f[R] const fast = cbor::schema<sensor>::unverified_path(owner);
.EE
.PP
\&../reference/schema/unverified_path.md lists what each form checks.
.PP
More: the bytes of a message, every check, the accessor in detail, the
typed array view, a memory budget and the cost of each call are in
advanced/schema.md.
